DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "PGcourse.pl");

Context("Numeric");

$ans = List(0, 1);

Context()->texStrings;
BEGIN_PGML
For what values of [`c`] will
[`` A = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 \\ c & c^2 \end{bmatrix}``] be invertible?

Answer: for all [`c`] such that [`c\neq`][_]{$ans}{5}  
If there is more than one value of [`c`], enter a list separated by commas.
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
The matrix [`\displaystyle A = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 \\ c & c^2 \end{bmatrix}`] is invertible provided the columns of [`A`] are linearly independent, which will be the case if [`c \neq c^2`]. Thus, we require that [`c\neq 0,1`].
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
